{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests","id":1128791,"title":"[Signs of Sorcery Open Dev] Grimoires - Why use Palimpsests?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-14T07:10:27-07:00","id":1128791,"title":"[Signs of Sorcery Open Dev] Grimoires - Why use Palimpsests?","content":"I generally like how <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">preview about Grimoires</a> from <b>Signs of Sorcery </b>are opening many new avenues in encoding spells or giving nice \u2018I tattooed this Rote in my flesh for more power\u2019. But I have large problem with illogicality how idea of Palimpsests is shown in it. For ease of discussion, here is spell that creates them quoted from preview.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Scribe Palimpsest (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022) </i></b><br /> <b><i>Practice:</i></b><i> Weaving </i><br /> <b><i>Primary Factor:</i></b><i> Potency </i><br /> <b><i>Cost:</i></b><i> 1 Mana </i><br /> <b><i>Withstand:</i></b><i> Total Arcanum dots used in the rote + 1 </i><br /> <b><i>Suggested Rote Skills:</i></b><i> Crafts, Expression, Occult </i><br /> <br /> <i>Like \u201cScribe Grimoire\u201d, this spell gives physical form to a single rote's symbols. A mage can </i><br /> <i>cast it multiple times to fill one vessel with many rotes. She does so using a previously-</i><br /> <i>scribed Grimoire with its contents erased, scrubbed, scribbled out, painted over, or otherwise </i><br /> <i>made unreadable. The Storyteller chooses one Arcanum when the character casts this spell. </i><br /> <i>Whenever a character later casts the rote from the completed Grimoire, it acts as though it </i><br /> <i>incorporated dots of the chosen Arcanum equal to this spell's Potency, creating unpredictable </i><br /> <i>blended effects. If the Storyteller chose an Arcanum already included in the rote, grant the </i><br /> <i>casting one free Reach instead. Rotes learned with Experiences from a palimpsest carry these </i><br /> <i>extra Arcana effects with them. </i><br /> <br /> <i>+1 Reach: For one point of Mana, the spell's Duration is Lasting.</i><br /> <br /> <b>In reality, I cannot envision in-setting Awakened characters using it, not to mention players wanting to cast</b> <b>it.</b> Here are reasons why:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It\u2019s 3<sup>rd</sup> dot Prime spell, when <i>Scribe Grimoire</i> \u2013 on which <i>Scribe Palimpsest </i>is based \u2013 it\u2019s 1<sup>st</sup> dot spell, doing ( mostly ) the same. Lower dot\u2019s, easier to cast, safer to use. And is not obvious \u2018PCs trap\u2019.</li> <li>Random chosen \u2018special effect\u2019, that character have no idea to foreseen \u2013 <b>WHY to create dangerous Palimpsests from previous Grimoires, than to simply make new Grimoire with standard effect in it, that maybe modified on Reach options by new creator?</b> Even Guardians of Veil would discourage of using Palimpsests Rotes if all they can give is \u2018wild magic\u2019 effect, not giving any true power to Palimpsests users.</li> </ol>Now, I understand story-wise perspective on this is spell \u2013 it\u2019s are made to make \u2018dangerous Grimoires\u2019 that players want to use. But mechanics ( for now ) simply are not the worth the risk.<br /> <br /> My propositions on how to change <b><i>Scribe Palimpsest</i></b> spell:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Creator of Palimpsest can feel what Arcana effects can be in it before finalizing Palimpsest \u2013 it\u2019s not perfect and Abyssal forces are known to temper with False Grimoires to spread as Palimpsests, but creator can more or less sense how new Grimoire will work, without exact details.</li> </ol>AND/OR<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Created Palimpsests have twice the Potency spent on them \u2013 new Grimoire is \u2018hungry\u2019 for power previous version had, making it much more powerful easily. BUT Palimpsests are known for having weird, unforeseen effects encoded in them.</li> </ol>One or both of those ideas make creating Palimpsests much more plausible in-setting and much more probable for players to try this \u2018dangerous road\u2019 of previous spells in same Grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:31:58-07:00","id":1128802,"title":"","content":"Even if the rider effects are unpredictable you will typically know what you're getting into just based on the arcana that the random effect is derived from. Oh, also, it's easy to run it not as wild magic, and instead as an extra arcana rider effect that's unknown until the first time the spell is cast, after that it remains static.<br /> <br /> Second, a palimpsest that has the same arcana as the rote inscribed over it grants a free Reach over and above usual Reach limits instead of a random arcana effect, which is a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:40:31-07:00","id":1128807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128802#post1128802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the rider effects are unpredictable you will typically know what you're getting into just based on the arcana that the random effect is derived from.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can predict spells effects <b><i>without</i></b> using them in the first place? I first heard about it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128802#post1128802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also, it's easy to run it not as wild magic, and instead as an extra arcana rider effect that's unknown until the first time the spell is cast, after that it remains static.</div> </div> </div> </div>You found Palimpsest in some Time Before Temple or some deceased very private solitaire collection - You just use it and risk getting killed or your friends on first try? Unknown magic is most dangerous magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128802#post1128802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, a palimpsest that has the same arcana as the rote inscribed over it grants a free Reach over and above usual Reach limits instead of a random arcana effect, which is a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have 10% chance for getting it beneficial and (almost) 100% of possible denegerous effect - I would argue that Guardians find it's far to low to test those numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:05:26-07:00","id":1128825,"title":"","content":"Use Time and cast Momentary Flux to determine if the spell is good or bad for you. Use Mage Sight to examine the text before casting a spell from it.<br /> <br /> Palimpsest are obviously there to be interesting enough to serve as a Mystery. The unwise Mage uses it without taking safety precautions, the wise Mage figured out how to get a beneficial boost to their magic.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you're missing something so obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:23:56-07:00","id":1128835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128825#post1128825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Time and cast Momentary Flux to determine if the spell is good or bad for you. Use Mage Sight to examine the text before casting a spell from it.<br /> <br /> Palimpsest are obviously there to be interesting enough to serve as a Mystery. The unwise Mage uses it without taking safety precautions, the wise Mage figured out how to get a beneficial boost to their magic.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you're missing something so obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>In logical Awakening setting - <i>there <b>will be none</b> Palimpsests in use if the spell will be as show in preview.</i> Wise mages would not produce them - even on beneficial Rotes, they can create dangerous effects - better just use create normal Grimoire. And Palimpsests from Left-Hand mages just end up in Censorium the moment they are found as they are assumed to have malignant effects. If Palimpsests will not have anything <i>really</i> beneficial to use them constant - I really do not see mages using them instead of classical Grimoires. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:31:53-07:00","id":1128842,"title":"","content":"Yes, they would, -FREE- Reach is a damn good reason to make or use a palimpsest. Also, that extra arcana rider? You don't need to have the arcana in question to get the effect. So say you want to cast a spell that would benefit from Time and Matter, but you don't have Matter. If you have the right spell from the right palimpsest you don't need Matter to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> You're just looking at this all wrong man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:35:43-07:00","id":1128844,"title":"","content":"Oh, also, a Palimpsest is created by a spell, are you honestly going to tell me that Mages don't know how to sufficiently analyze their own magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:56:34-07:00","id":1128848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128842#post1128842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they would, -FREE- Reach is a damn good reason to make or use a palimpsest.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 Free Reach is like... meh? It's only 1-3 Mana points for mitigating Paradox from one extra Reach over your normal Paradox pool in Gnosis 1-6 mage characters ( i.e. those that most games are run ). Instead of free casting, you can have like 3-4 per game session from Gnosis 1 characters ( with no other hand sources of Mana with them, like Artifacts, Imbued Items, Familiars, legacy Oblations... )<br /> <br /> AND, for Palimpsests it's for the 1/10 of all items. It's <i>really, really, really </i>low number of benefits to how 'wild magic' things those items can create. As Guardian I would only said to all around me saying: <i>'You see, using Palimpsests is really stupid idea when you can just create safe new Grimoire ( for us ).'</i><br /> <br /> Once again - I'm not agaisnt Palimpsests idea itself per se - rather I found shown mechanics of creation then totally underpowered and/or unplayable in real game ( beside ST story hooks for NPC only ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128842#post1128842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that extra arcana rider? You don't need to have the arcana in question to get the effect. So say you want to cast a spell that would benefit from Time and Matter, but you don't have Matter. If you have the right spell from the right palimpsest you don't need Matter to cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>WHY would I need 'another Arcana for effect' of spell? </b>Almost all spells in 2E corebook are 1 Arcanum effects. Those that use 2 Arcana, are spells <i>specifilcy</i> made to transform things - you know, spells <i>you want to be sure you are changed/will things change into</i> by casting. 'Random other Arcana' is totally unneeded in casting spells, leading only to 'wild magic' kind of things. I would even say it's less realible than Paradox - Abyss influance you can at least mitigate with Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128842#post1128842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're just looking at this all wrong man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you forget how 2E spells and magic rules are written when not taking those things in consideration. Many times I was hearing 'Acanthus Time Wars are totally thing as they are possible mechanically' - well, things I wrote about now will be gameplay with Palimpsests spell above going with 2E Mage corebook spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128844#post1128844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also, a Palimpsest is created by a spell, are you honestly going to tell me that Mages don't know how to sufficiently analyze their own magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>BEFORE casting this spell? Yes, totally they do not know other's spell imbued in Palimpsests. They senes 'Oh, in this item it's Arcanum's X Rote of Y Parcatice - but what exactly it is? Probably something with Symbol Z - but what?'<br /> <br /> Even if they would know exactly what encoded Rote should do - 'encoding random effects' of Palimpsets are there to put them on mines. <i>'Dear Ruling Council, I did not know this Healing Rote is having also Transmute Into Stone effect on it, I swear...'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:01:42-07:00","id":1128851,"title":"","content":"What exactly it does would be spelled out in Deep Information, this is exactly the kind of thing that Scrutiny is for.<br /> <br /> Also, I guess you haven't noticed, but the previews for SOS have spells that are conjunctions. Which is what you could use a Palimpsest for.<br /> <br /> By the way, you keep bringing up Guardians as being prejudiced against these, but it didn't say that in the text, so it's safe to assume they're not against them by default. If we are going to bring Guardians into this though, hey, you might feel ambivalent about free Reach, but a Guardian would be super excited about it.<br /> <br /> And yes, the chances of finding a useful palimpsest are rare, that's why you have Mages fighting over every single one of them to find the good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-14-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:03:23-07:00","id":1128862,"title":"","content":"So, I just reread the bit on palimpsest, and it specifically says that the scraps of previous rites in the palimpsest that creates those extra magical effects are Mysteries with Opacity. The significance of this is that yes, a Mage can determine exactly what a spell out of a palimpsest will do before casting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T11:46:38-07:00","id":1128895,"title":"","content":"I thought that Palimpets effects are determined each time that rote are cast, and that Scrap Mysteries are there to decode the spells that got overwritten to create palimpet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:01:54-07:00","id":1128899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128895#post1128895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that Palimpets effects are determined each time that rote are cast, and that Scrap Mysteries are there to decode the spells that got overwritten to create palimpet?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a misconception on my part, but I assume the results of blending two rotes into a palimpsest is what's producing unpredictable results (Especially since it apparently varies by Potency), but with exploration of the rote at varying levels of Potency those effects can be discovered and nailed down. <br /> <br /> I also don't see why you wouldn't be able to nail these effects down before experimenting via casting. You might be right about Scrap Mysteries though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:29:19-07:00","id":1128912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Whenever a character later casts the rote from the completed Grimoire, it acts as though it </i><br /> <i>incorporated dots of the chosen Arcanum equal to this spell's Potency, creating unpredictable </i><br /> <i>blended effects. </i> </div> </div> </div>This might be a language thing, but it gave me an impression that the unpredictable blended effects are checked for at &quot;when rote is being cast&quot;, so they could vary with each use. i hope it's not the case, because i think that static twisted rotes have great potential to be insanely cool, and if im going to play mage again, i will probably roll a Grimoire Specialist using palimpsests as &quot;dirty&quot; power used to bridge the difference between her and more experienced, more powerful mages.<br /> My GM though straight said that it's static twisted effect or no palimpsests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:53:50-07:00","id":1128928,"title":"","content":"It's the only thing that makes sense to me otherwise it makes half of the &quot;benefit&quot; of the spell useless and a palimpsest will only get used for the extra Reach, which is cool but the twisted arcana effect you can rely on seems like it would be the cool hook that makes you want to get your hands on as many palimpsest as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:07:53-07:00","id":1128934,"title":"","content":"From GM perspective, it's much less taxing and easier to figure out 2, 3 or even 10 specific palimpsets in advance between games (your player says he will make a palimpset out of rote XYZ; you look at it really hard, then figure out if there is intuitive cool rider for it, if not you roll to check for inspiration from seeing randomly generated combo, and if not...i guess the +1 reach option is really boring, even if efficient), than to come up with them on spot each time a twisted rote is cast, so...yeah.<br /> And to be fair, it seems fairly easy to get a lot of them even with starting character, especially if you get Prime 3 and some Order Status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:08:36-07:00","id":1128935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128862#post1128862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I just reread the bit on palimpsest, and it specifically says that the scraps of previous rites in the palimpsest that creates those extra magical effects are Mysteries with Opacity. The significance of this is that yes, a Mage can determine exactly what a spell out of a palimpsest will do before casting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compared two pieces of text about Palimpsests and they are a bit contradicting themselves here - before there is:<br /> <br /> <i>'A mage can glean scraps of the rotes inscribed previously in a palimpsest through the echoes of their Pattern, though she can never learn them with Experiences. Once she's figured out how to cast these echoes, she can develop her own rotes based on those spells. Each rote echo is its own Mystery with Opacity equal to the total Arcana dots used in the rote + 1 for every century that has passed since its original inscription, to a maximum of +5. Once she has fully scrutinized the echo with Focused Mage Sight, she may cast it from the Grimoire with a two-die penalty to her spellcasting roll. '</i><br /> <br /> Here 'spell echoes' are treated as Mysteries based on previous Rotes - clear Rote, clear effect, recasted in modern times. Simple idea - one spell that you can 'uncover' under the original Grimoire.<br /> <br /> On the <i>Scribe Palimpsest</i> spell itself we have this:<br /> <br /> <i>'She does so using a previously-scribed Grimoire with its contents erased, scrubbed, scribbled out, painted over, or otherwise made unreadable. The Storyteller chooses one Arcanum when the character casts this spell. Whenever a character later casts the rote from the completed Grimoire, it acts as though it incorporated dots of the chosen Arcanum equal to this spell's Potency, creating unpredictable blended effects.'</i><br /> <br /> Here what in previous quote was 'spell echoes' is totally missed and added is 'wild magic' effect - <b>Maybe it's only wording thing but it's sounds as <i>Scribe Palimpsest</i> totally miss the previous Rotes content of previous version of Grimoire. </b><br /> <br /> <b>I suppose that end rules will assume 'spell echoes' incorporation as needed to cast <i>Scribe Palimpsest</i> and, in reality, <i>Scribe</i> spell will get you conjuncted second Rote on those that you write, yes?</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Example: </b></i>You have old Grimoire about magical plant rising, with Life spells about it. When you made this book into Palimpsest about Forces magic control of fire, you will get Control Fire Rote, that when cast - activates also Plant Rising spell in the target.<br /> <br /> Am I reading it right here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:17:13-07:00","id":1128936,"title":"","content":"You know, we cant really judge palimpsets without having full rules on adding optional arcana to a spell - something that i heard could be expanded upon in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:27:53-07:00","id":1128940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128936#post1128936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, we cant really judge palimpsets without having full rules on adding optional spells to arcana - something that i heard could be expanded upon in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? If I understand concept correctly ( going with 'spell echoes' idea ), Palimpsests are things like this:<br /> <br /> We have Grimoire book, let's say it has 500 years. In previous version it was Grimoire A, with 5 Rotes A. Now it's scrapped clean. All Rotes A are becoming 'spell echoes' on the book itself. Then comes Mystygoug or Libertaine and he records his Grimoire B with 5 Rotes B. Now, all Rotes B are in reality connected spells of Rote A and Rote B of particular Grimoire idea.<br /> <br /> So this works if in our example Grimoire A is about 'Magical plantation' and Grimoire B are 'Forces attack spells' - we end with Palimpsest's final 'Forces attack spells that increase growth of plants' spells. All of which we simple can have from 2E corebook. In 2E rules Grimoire is just magical list of Rotes - you just pick up number of spells and put them in to book/DVD disk/write in to the stone/whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:39:11-07:00","id":1128947,"title":"","content":"I want to point out that to create Palimpsests - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palimpsest\" target=\"_blank\">like real world term in textual studies</a> - you need to have original text of scroll to use it. In <b>Mage</b>, it simply maybe that you need to have <i>vague idea of previous version of Grimoire what Rotes have in it</i>, i.e. general theme of magical book - to create your Palimpsests effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Key here is that those should be 'spell echoes' of previous magic in it - not totally unrelated random effects going only from Arcana.</b> If Palimpsest was previously book about magical plant growth, all new Rotes in it should also do some wild plant growth, even when caster may not be sure 100% what will be where growing. To make spell usable on game sessions and Awakened world - it should be at least somehow predictable from 'spell echoes', not totally random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:49:18-07:00","id":1128968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128940#post1128940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? </div> </div> </div> </div>Because any judgements that are made are entirely based on supposition and guesswork, which are very easy to get wrong. Unless someone can tap into Dave's brain, we have no idea how the systems is supposed to work, what it's intericacies are, and how we can fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:11:39-07:00","id":1128973,"title":"","content":"It's threads like these that make developers leery of posting in-progress previews.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone ever make a Palimpsest? Because they're goldfishing for new rotes they can't normally create. Because they're magical radicals that like to force change and shake things up. Because the grimoire with the old rotes can't simply be erased completely but is itself a rare item that enhances rotes written in it making it worth reusing even with some added chaos.<br /> <br /> You don't know the context, you haven't seen the rest of the book, stop trying to redesign things you don't understand and stop trying to foist your own non-standard interpretations of factions into the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:21:09-07:00","id":1128978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't know the context, you haven't seen the rest of the book, stop trying to redesign things you don't understand and stop trying to foist your own non-standard interpretations of factions into the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we please put this as a header at the top of the forums? Please? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:32:34-07:00","id":1128985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Example: </b></i>You have old Grimoire about magical plant rising, with Life spells about it. When you made this book into Palimpsest about Forces magic control of fire, you will get Control Fire Rote, that when cast - activates also Plant Rising spell in the target.<br /> <br /> Am I reading it right here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's obvious this is incorrect, because your example is a combined spell and that isn't what a palimpsest does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128947#post1128947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to point out that to create Palimpsests - <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palimpsest&quot;]like</a> real world term in textual studies[/URL] - you need to have original text of scroll to use it. In <b>Mage</b>, it simply maybe that you need to have <i>vague idea of previous version of Grimoire what Rotes have in it</i>, i.e. general theme of magical book - to create your Palimpsests effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You rewrite over a cleaned up original text, so obviously the magical version works like the mundane in terms of this. You do not &quot;just need a vague idea of previous version of grimoire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-14-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:14:38-07:00","id":1129004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's threads like these that make developers leery of posting in-progress previews.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone ever make a Palimpsest? Because they're goldfishing for new rotes they can't normally create. Because they're magical radicals that like to force change and shake things up. Because the grimoire with the old rotes can't simply be erased completely but is itself a rare item that enhances rotes written in it making it worth reusing even with some added chaos.<br /> <br /> You don't know the context, you haven't seen the rest of the book, stop trying to redesign things you don't understand and <b>stop trying to foist your own non-standard interpretations of factions into the books.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That bolded part? That, seriously. People need to stop doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T21:58:44-07:00","id":1129113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's threads like these that make developers leery of posting in-progress previews.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand Open Devs process, it's there to show places that may need rewriting/fixing before actual release. Like at least wording on Palimpsests spell, in this case. I assumed - just like with Code for Hunter 2E preview we saw few days earlier - idea is that fans will discuss rules in now version of the books, so devs can see if there is no clash in development versions of rules. Like it was done to all 2E Vampire supplements, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would anyone ever make a Palimpsest? Because they're goldfishing for new rotes they can't normally create.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, just show in end rules WHAT kind of weird Rote they can make - writing something like 'creating unpredictable blended effects' is saying nothing about nature of the newly created power. It should point here to the idea of 'spell echoes', introduced earlier in outside spell's text, if I understand intend here correctly ( from whole paragrah eralier on 'solving' what previouse Grimoire was really doing. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're magical radicals that like to force change and shake things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those kind of items end in Censorium... And people are at least meet by Guardians of the Veil. One thing is 'do magic with some extra flair'. Another is totally random effects add to previous non-harm spells. Like my example of Healing Rote with added Turn into Stone random effect from previous Palimpsests ( even if previous Grimoire was also about Healing, not turning people into stone ).<br /> <br /> If power is totally random, it really would be logical for Guardians to ban this kind dangerous practices. Even Scelesti are passed once or twice in mage life if there is position they would not do much harm - still, there is possibility that adding Abyss to the spell will open the whole Hell loose - and we here are having similar idea. <i>IF the wording of 'unpredictable blended effects' means total 'wild magic'...</i><br /> <br /> If whole Palimpsests idea is based on 'spell echoes' of previous versions of Grimoire, the spell itself should be re-written before release.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the grimoire with the old rotes can't simply be erased completely but is itself a rare item that enhances rotes written in it making it worth reusing even with some added chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not against this idea itself - I like it as ST, even - but I'm against vagueness of rules written for it now. Like literally in this very topic we have at least 3 very different readings of those text pieces, by me, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, all based on the same text.<br /> <br /> I know it's test version of rules, but it's not clear on the execution of them. I assume it means to re-use 'spell echoes' from the document's sections earlier, but spell read on it's own easily can lead to 'wild magic' effects in created Palimpsests, without pointing this in it\u2019s text.<br /> <br /> And as we got whole section on Grimoires, I assume we will not see more clarifications on this in other parts of book - because of word count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't know the context,</div> </div> </div> </div>We got whole Grimoires section - at least from the looks of it - we will not see more in this supplement on those items. It's only one of many topics <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> are said to talk to - so there will not be extra place to 'and when were talking about Palimpsets in Grimoires section, we really meant it this'. Just like was in 2E Secrets of Covenants. ( Not too mention that idea of clarifying rules outside their rules chapter would be simple stupid. ) So no, we see whole context on the subject - there will (almost sure) nothing more on it in the book.<br /> <br /> We just see it's confusing written here, for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you haven't seen the rest of the book, stop trying to redesign things you don't understand</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again - What is point of Open Dev if not pointing rules that could need re-writening before the actual release of books? Just to see what devs are planning for us to show in year or two? For this would simply Table of Contents be enough. If you show test version of rules to fans before realese \u2013 it\u2019s to point out problems with them. Like any \u2018open beta\u2019 of modern intellectual content \u2013 is it video game, RPG game or anything.<br /> <br /> Next on the stance of Guardians of Veil on <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">using unpredictable magic....</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T22:21:03-07:00","id":1129116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1128973#post1128973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and stop trying to foist your own non-standard interpretations of factions into the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own interpretation you say? Let\u2019s look what Guardians say about using unpredictable magic\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dMtAw 2E, Guardians write-up, p. 39\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You see what I\u2019m saying. I can see it spreading across your face like a fire crawling across dry logs. Are you stopping for the night, or are you still thinking of ways you could get more than a few bucks? Another spell tells you the credit card numbers of everyone in the restaurant, who\u2019s there on a date, who\u2019s rich yet vulnerable.<br /> <br /> How long until you try something that really bites you? Where does the line get drawn? <b>When would you stop caring about the damage your magic brings to the world? Is your fire something that needs to be tended carefully, or something that could gutter out to ashes and embers</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dGotV book, p. 49\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Protect the Sanctity of Magic</b><br /> Guardians of the Veil do their best to ensure that only the worthy master magic\u2019s secrets. Other orders resent the Guardians\u2019 interference, but recognize that <b>they perform a valuable service by keeping dangerous magic from novices</b> and fools and testing the Sleepers who would touch the Watchtowers. The Inheritors (see p. 135) and Ordeal Keepers (see p. 143) are the most enthusiastic adherents of this cause, but all Guardians do their part.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dGotV book, p. 50\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Finally, the order publicly preaches against the overuse of vulgar magic. It\u2019s a security threat </b>and a potential doorway into the Abyss. Mages who constantly incur Paradoxes or overuse vulgar Arts are \ufb01rst in line to be tested when the caucus arranges new ordeals.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not have Vulgar magic in system \u2013 but random, Paradox-like effects inducing Rotes from 'wrong' Palipsests are as close to it that it can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dGotV book, p. 137\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When dealing with sloppy or indiscreet mages, the goals of the Inheritors are, in some ways, the opposite of those of the Mysterium. Whereas the mystagogues are dedicated to discovering ancient lore and treasures and returning them to the hands of the Awakened, <b>Inheritors are dedicated to taking that selfsame lore and those precise treasures out of the hands of mages who turn the treasures to \ufb02ashy or hubristic ends, use them for frivolous purposes or otherwise abuse them</b>. The Inheritors do this only with the greatest stealth and discretion, of course. While there are those among the Awakened who already suspect the Guardians of the Veil of taking an excessively parental role in the affairs of the Awakened, being caught relieving a mage of a favored toy (or, worse, his life) would remove all doubt and put the Guardians in general in a particularly fragile position, politically speaking.<br /> (\u2026)<br /> Inheritors clearly feel that magic should be even harder to master than it already is. As they see it, <b>stupid mages are a dime a dozen, </b>and it\u2019s their hubris that is to blame for the strength of the Abyss \u2014 <b>a problem that would not exist were all Awakened as discreet in their use of magic as the Guardians of the Veil.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that I made a point that Guardians are very much against using unpredictable \u2013 and by this, possibly dangerous \u2013 magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2017, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T22:55:15-07:00","id":1129119,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between asking for clarity, e.g. <b>is the effect of the Palimpsest rote different each time it is used, or random but fixed? Can the effect be determined before casting? If not, how would watchdog groups such as the Guardians of the Veil react to such consistently unpredictable magic? Will there be suggestions for the ST or players on why Palimpsests might be desirable to create?</b> and what you wrote.<br /> <br /> Unless you spot an actual <i>factual error</i> you probably shouldn't be proposing direct changes, you're not a game designer and you don't know what the lead dev actually has in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the GotV: there's a difference between keeping dangerous stuff out of the hands of novices and trying to stop Masters (y'know, the people capable of inscribing Grimoires) from investigating Mysteries. [edit]Meant creating new rotes, anyone not a Master will be copying from another Grimoire and would be easier to police.[/edit]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 08-15-2017, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T02:19:07-07:00","id":1129153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129119#post1129119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between asking for clarity, e.g. <b>is the effect of the Palimpsest rote different each time it is used, or random but fixed? Can the effect be determined before casting? If not, how would watchdog groups such as the Guardians of the Veil react to such consistently unpredictable magic? Will there be suggestions for the ST or players on why Palimpsests might be desirable to create?</b> and what you wrote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those arguments and questions rose AFTER I created topic, when my view was clashed with WHW and Mrmdubois. Probably should not proposed solutions on Opening Post, but the problem is still not resolved \u2013 <b>HOW Palimpsests rules are there to be used, in the end? </b>Wording of the spell implies random effect on creation ( or even totally random effects on each usage ), \u2018spell echoes\u2019 section imply that there should be based on previous content of the Grimoire. Clearing those in rules on re-writing this section will be crucial before release.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129119#post1129119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you spot an actual <i>factual error</i> you probably shouldn't be proposing direct changes, you're not a game designer and you don't know what the lead dev actually has in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules as vague as this ARE factual error \u2013 <i>literally</i> me, WHW and Mrmdubois needed to judge implementation it on the setting for 1,5 forum pages, and we still not find out one line, as two options are possible. If this section left as it is now, it <i>will lead</i> to many needless debates at game tables. Not to mention that one of interpretation of it leads to totally illogical game setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129119#post1129119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the GotV: there's a difference between keeping dangerous stuff out of the hands of novices and trying to stop Masters (y'know, the people capable of inscribing Grimoires) from investigating Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>To Guardians \u2013 no, there is not. Guardians are watching and then exposing irresponsible moves of Masters <i>all the time</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2019MtAw 2E, p.40\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All thrones are false; all souls are flawed</b><br /> Mages are inherently unworthy of the perfection of the Awakened City. Paradox is a sign of a mage\u2019s fundamental impurity, reflecting her sins. Yet if sins for a just end grant Wisdom, Guardians are therefore capable of transferring merit, leaving all other souls and Orders flawed in their ignorance. The Guardians consider it their duty to undermine charismatic leaders, <b>expose the faults of wise sages</b>, and force mages to doubt one another to remind them that their primary mission is to struggle with their own souls. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on final ruling of how Palimpsests effects will work \u2013 If they will be based on \u2018spell echoes\u2019 or totally random on creation but predictable in usage \u2013 or totally random each time \u2013 using them would go from \u2018Yes, take it and analyze rest of previous magic, good Mystery seeking\u2019 to \u2018We must lock every one of them in Censorium as it can once heal \u2013 and second time spread disease on city \u2013 and third time make sky burn\u2019. <b>It\u2019s irrelevant to Guardians if you are novice or Master \u2013 if you are using magic irresponsible, <i>you should be punished</i>.</b> Using items that generates random effects ( not possible to investigate earlier ) is exactly the thing Guardians would stop.<br /> <br /> And as Guardians have at least some political power in most settings, \u2018wild magic\u2019 Palimpsests would on creation will end in Censoria \u2013 or even be destroyed. If they would be stable effects based on \u2018spell echoes\u2019 \u2013 it\u2019s all good for the everyone to study or create them as Mysteries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T02:29:53-07:00","id":1129155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129119#post1129119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the GotV: there's a difference between keeping dangerous stuff out of the hands of novices and trying to stop Masters (y'know, the people capable of inscribing Grimoires) from investigating Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't hard to create Grimoires and Palimpsets. All you need to do is cast Scribe Grimoire (or otherwise get a Grimoire from other source), which is a 1st dot Prime spell, and then cast Scribe Palimpsest, which is a Prime 3 effect. It's somewhat mana intensive, but it's doable for novices - especially Obrimos starting characters, who can pick Prime 3 out of the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T02:33:54-07:00","id":1129157,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> You jumped to your conclusion after reading the spell without gathering any additional context from the section on palimpsest. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't actually think WHW and I are having a different interpretation of how they work. We had a brief clarifying conversation of what we got out of the text and essentially arrived at the same conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:13:01-07:00","id":1129161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129155#post1129155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really isn't hard to create Grimoires and Palimpsets. All you need to do is cast Scribe Grimoire (or otherwise get a Grimoire from other source), which is a 1st dot Prime spell, and then cast Scribe Palimpsest, which is a Prime 3 effect. It's somewhat mana intensive, but it's doable for novices - especially Obrimos starting characters, who can pick Prime 3 out of the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And depending on reading of Palimpsests spell, you can end up with novice mages on some 'atomic like' cancerous Rotes they themselves create. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh, sorry, they just need to 'copy' spells - 'nuke effect' is by 'accident'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2017, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:18:26-07:00","id":1129163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129155#post1129155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really isn't hard to create Grimoires and Palimpsets. All you need to do is cast Scribe Grimoire (or otherwise get a Grimoire from other source), which is a 1st dot Prime spell, and then cast Scribe Palimpsest, which is a Prime 3 effect. It's somewhat mana intensive, but it's doable for novices - especially Obrimos starting characters, who can pick Prime 3 out of the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the creation of the Rote itself is something that can only be done by Masters. So &quot;worst case&quot; you're looking at a novice Mage who's somehow gotten their hands on at least <i>two</i> Grimoires, and is willing to erase or deface one of them to experiment with magic beyond their ken.<br /> <br /> Will the GotV be pissy about that? Probably, if they find out. But society frowns on things like underage drinking and that happens all the time. My main point to wyrdhamster was that there is a group that will be creating these Palimpsests that the Guardians won't be inclined to bother and that said group has legitimate interest in creating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:27:09-07:00","id":1129165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129153#post1129153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those arguments and questions rose AFTER I created topic, when my view was clashed with WHW and Mrmdubois. Probably should not proposed solutions on Opening Post, but the problem is still not resolved \u2013 <b>HOW Palimpsests rules are there to be used, in the end? </b>Wording of the spell implies random effect on creation ( or even totally random effects on each usage ), \u2018spell echoes\u2019 section imply that there should be based on previous content of the Grimoire. Clearing those in rules on re-writing this section will be crucial before release.</div> </div> </div> </div>The questions I proposed were crafted solely from the &quot;issues&quot; you raised in your opening post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules as vague as this ARE factual error \u2013 <i>literally</i> me, WHW and Mrmdubois needed to judge implementation it on the setting for 1,5 forum pages, and we still not find out one line, as two options are possible. If this section left as it is now, it <i>will lead</i> to many needless debates at game tables. Not to mention that one of interpretation of it leads to totally illogical game setting. </div> </div> </div>No, a &quot;factual error&quot; is like in the M:tAw 2e beta where the spell <i>Transmission</i> declared &quot;WiFi&quot;, &quot;bluetooth&quot;, and &quot;radio waves&quot; different things when they are, in fact, all radio waves.<br /> <br /> What you want is <i>clarification. </i>You don't know what's wrong or right because you don't even understand what's being said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To Guardians \u2013 no, there is not. Guardians are watching and then exposing irresponsible moves of Masters <i>all the time</i>. </div> </div> </div>To a Guardian, yes, yes there is a difference. Also watching Masters is very different than interfering with their work. This is the kind of shit I meant by foisting your own interpretation off on everyone else. We know, from the fiction and other sources, that Guardians are just as constrained by local politics as everyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on final ruling of how Palimpsests effects will work \u2013 If they will be based on \u2018spell echoes\u2019 or totally random on creation but predictable in usage \u2013 or totally random each time \u2013 using them would go from \u2018Yes, take it and analyze rest of previous magic, good Mystery seeking\u2019 to \u2018We must lock every one of them in Censorium as it can once heal \u2013 and second time spread disease on city \u2013 and third time make sky burn\u2019. <b>It\u2019s irrelevant to Guardians if you are novice or Master \u2013 if you are using magic irresponsible, <i>you should be punished</i>.</b> Using items that generates random effects ( not possible to investigate earlier ) is exactly the thing Guardians would stop.<br /> <br /> And as Guardians have at least some political power in most settings, \u2018wild magic\u2019 Palimpsests would on creation will end in Censoria \u2013 or even be destroyed. If they would be stable effects based on \u2018spell echoes\u2019 \u2013 it\u2019s all good for the everyone to study or create them as Mysteries. </div> </div> </div>And you're once again extrapolating from nothing. <b>Ask for clarification</b>, don't tell someone how to do their job when you're clueless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:45:29-07:00","id":1129167,"title":"","content":"By the way, when I was talking about full context, I wasn't talking about more grimoire rules. I was talking about adding Arcana to a spell beyond it's basic minimum - like you do with many spirit-related spells to extend their influence to also include ghosts, goetia, etc. So there is a chance we will see some examples and rules about doing things like that to other spells; maybe, lets say, you can add Death to spells in order to make them affect Ghostly Twilight, and a twisted rote that rolled &quot;Death&quot; on its twisted roll could end up being an accidental ghostbusting spell - still doing what it did previously, but with a twist.<br /> If there isn't anything like that, I'm going to have troubles with coming up with these, because it's hard to do for me and my GM without having much to extrapolate from. But maybe there is something that will make it more intuitive in the book, because I think (but I might be misremembering) that more complicated, multi-arcana spells were supposed to have some space in this book too.<br /> Or maybe in the next one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T03:52:31-07:00","id":1129169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129163#post1129163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the creation of the Rote itself is something that can only be done by Masters. So &quot;worst case&quot; you're looking at a novice Mage who's somehow gotten their hands on at least <i>two</i> Grimoires, and is willing to erase or deface one of them to experiment with magic beyond their ken.<br /> <br /> Will the GotV be pissy about that? Probably, if they find out. But society frowns on things like underage drinking and that happens all the time. My main point to wyrdhamster was that there is a group that will be creating these Palimpsests that the Guardians won't be inclined to bother and that said group has legitimate interest in creating them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, you can always Scribe Grimoire of a Rote you personally know, you don't need to invent new ones. Getting your hands on new grimoires is also fairly easy, because their Merit cost is very cheap; it's pretty believable to see a Mage use their temporary status requisition to temporarily get dots worth of Grimoires, copy them using Scribe Grimoire, and then copy copies to create palimpsets over the copies until something interesting is generated. I tried to play something like this before these rules, and it ended up being cool, but not worth it in most cases; Cognoscente finally makes it worth the mana, time and potentially willpower investment to actually Grimoire-ize your rotes; Palimpsets can make it potentially rewarding to palimpset-ize some of your non-rote assets too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T04:12:56-07:00","id":1129173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129169#post1129169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I tried to play something like this before these rules, and it ended up being cool, but not worth it in most cases; Cognoscente finally makes it worth the mana, time and potentially willpower investment to actually Grimoire-ize your rotes; Palimpsets can make it potentially rewarding to palimpset-ize some of your non-rote assets too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it all depend how 'random' Palimpsests effects can be. With those rules I easily can see starting character with Prime 3 that takes her favorite Grimoire from Order and copy over and over again Rotes she knows and can cast - for each repitition all spells in first Grimoire will get +1 Free Reach. One Free Reach is not something very good - but after 3rd repitition of Palimpsets on same book, we see Rotes with +3 Free Reach - and THIS is really powerful. Then question is how 'random' those effects with each iteration will be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T04:22:17-07:00","id":1129176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129173#post1129173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it all depend how 'random' Palimpsests effects can be. With those rules I easily can see starting character with Prime 3 that takes her favorite Grimoire from Order and copy over and over again Rotes she knows and can cast - for each repitition all spells in first Grimoire will get +1 Free Reach. One Free Reach is not something very good - but after 3rd repitition of Palimpsets on same book, we see Rotes with +3 Free Reach - and THIS is really powerful. Then question is how 'random' those effects with each iteration will be...</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> Where do you get the idea that you can go for +3 from? You cast Scribe Palimpsest, Arcana to &quot;borrow from&quot; is determined upon completion of the scribing process, and if it's the same as the Arcanum of Palimpset, you get +1 Reach.<br /> If you create another Palimpset on a corpse of a old Palimpset...you will repeat the process, I don't think it will stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T04:47:42-07:00","id":1129180,"title":"","content":"Agreed, there isn't any indication that the free Reach effect stacks with itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T06:54:31-07:00","id":1129206,"title":"","content":"It does seem fairly trivial to create a palimpsest with the free reach effect - just scribe a rote, erase it, and then inscribe it again. <br /> <br /> <i>Unless, </i>of course, a palimpsest can display arcarna that <i>none of the rotes previously encoded on it contained</i>. That, to me, sounds like it could be a really interesting mystery. and may be one reason mages experiment with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T09:28:47-07:00","id":1129266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129206#post1129206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Unless, </i>of course, a palimpsest can display arcarna that <i>none of the rotes previously encoded on it contained</i>. That, to me, sounds like it could be a really interesting mystery. and may be one reason mages experiment with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then we go in to 'wild magic' area where Palimpsets effects are not related to previous Grimoire content - and we have whole discussion about Guardians being against them all over again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T09:41:03-07:00","id":1129271,"title":"","content":"Palimpsests not being bound to only &quot;do&quot; the Arcanum that was previously inscribed on the grimoire seems to be the thing, because Scribe Palimpsest doesn't instruct you to pick from Arcana composing spells previously inscribed there. Which, honestly, is better, because instead of making Palimpsest one specific thing, it allows Palimpsests to be that *and* tons of other interesting cases.<br /> Guardians also are not some kind of omnipotent secret police killing you for creating a Palimpsest or casting a Paradox-risking spell. Lets not turn them all into some kind of genocidal murderkillers who can delegalize whole branches of magic willy-nilly because half of the corebook spells would end up being Bad Wrong Magicfun.<br /> Static Palimpsests that do not necessarily are related to previous content of Grimoire don't really have to be super murder dangerous. I mean, if you create a Palimpsest which you think isn't fit for use, you just *don't spend a Willpower point to safely unleash it* and just try again, until you hit something that suits your fancy. It's kind of like in some cRPG games, you can apply a wild card power up to your item, and then keep rerolling it until you either are satisfied with it or run out of resources to keep rerolling. <br /> So I think that you are overreacting; I don't think that adding even 5 dots of another Arcanum to the spell (note it's not adding a COMBINED spell to the effect, it seems its more like how adding Spirit or Death to &quot;Scribe Grimoire&quot; can turn it into &quot;Haunted Grimoire&quot;) will end up accidentally killing you when you try out the spell before deciding if the Palimpsest is &quot;ready&quot; to be properly and safely added to your inventory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:00:44-07:00","id":1129281,"title":"","content":"@WHW for a Reach and a mana a palimpsest is Lasting, so no WP expenditure.<br /> <br /> Anyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> your opinion of the Guardian's reaction is way overblown. They don't have a problem with randomness, they have a problem with carelessness. It's possible to be careful while dealing with random outcomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:04:33-07:00","id":1129283,"title":"","content":"I forgot! Yeah, so its even easier to not end up with a terrible palimpsest, just overwrite it until you end up with something interesting (in-game point of view), or just ask your GM how much time and mana points until you get something interesting (out of game point of view).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:37:39-07:00","id":1129396,"title":"","content":"I will write it in the opening of post - Having Palimsest 'special powers' based on 'spell echoes' would solve all those problems I rise - as those are making semi-reliable more powerful Grimoires on second take. Other random ideas, well - see below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129271#post1129271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Palimpsests not being bound to only &quot;do&quot; the Arcanum that was previously inscribed on the grimoire seems to be the thing, because Scribe Palimpsest doesn't instruct you to pick from Arcana composing spells previously inscribed there. Which, honestly, is better, because instead of making Palimpsest one specific thing, it allows Palimpsests to be that *and* tons of other interesting cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh, need to number Arcana from 1 to 10 then to roll on creating Palimpsests for each time it's used. And have 'Random Palimpsests Effects Table' if ever going to run them in Mage... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cause players will ask 'I make it till I get Free Reach +1 - or something not killing everyone in nearby that is interesting.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129271#post1129271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians also are not some kind of omnipotent secret police killing you for creating a Palimpsest or casting a Paradox-risking spell. Lets not turn them all into some kind of genocidal murderkillers who can delegalize whole branches of magic willy-nilly because half of the corebook spells would end up being Bad Wrong Magicfun.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Till Guardians do not get you - you have your fun. But in settings like Guardians ruled London, total random Palimpsests would be ban on creation on sight. Using <i>possible</i> tainted magic in many cases is enough to penalty it's use in public.<br /> <br /> 2. Half of corebook spells ARE Bad Wrong Magicfun - they risk your Wisdom or lead you to immoral actions. Really looking, anything from 3+ dots and not connected to Ephemera Beings or Realms IS questionable magic that can lead to problematic consequences for PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129271#post1129271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Static Palimpsests that do not necessarily are related to previous content of Grimoire don't really have to be super murder dangerous. I mean, if you create a Palimpsest which you think isn't fit for use, you just *don't spend a Willpower point to safely unleash it* and just try again, until you hit something that suits your fancy. It's kind of like in some cRPG games, you can apply a wild card power up to your item, and then keep rerolling it until you either are satisfied with it or run out of resources to keep rerolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. It's D&amp;D-esque 'I make it till I get something cool in the table'. It's really burdensome to ST. Becuase it will end in gameplay like this...<br /> - Player: 'I do this till Palimpsests effect will be good'<br /> - Storyteller: 'What do you mean 'will be good'?'<br /> - Player: 'I dunno, good for me'.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. Mage is not cRPG with Random Effects Table - even those from Paradox Reach are introduced as special, particular ideas, connected to particular levels of Paradox intensity. Now Palimpsests special effects look like Big Random Table without showing the Table to us in rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129271#post1129271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think that you are overreacting; I don't think that adding even 5 dots of another Arcanum to the spell (note it's not adding a COMBINED spell to the effect, it seems its more like how adding Spirit or Death to &quot;Scribe Grimoire&quot; can turn it into &quot;Haunted Grimoire&quot;) will end up accidentally killing you when you try out the spell before deciding if the Palimpsest is &quot;ready&quot; to be properly and safely added to your inventory.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand it should - you try truly random effects, one of them should be killable character or those around you. On the other hand - if you will have this kind dangerous effects, it will kill those around you - then Guardians will be totally right in taking away any possible made Palimpsest. So, in gameplay reality, only positive effects will have sense for players created Palimpsests - so it's nothing really thrilling me as ST - you will either have Palimpsests ban in setting cause they are to dangerous to use. Or they will be only willy-nilly positive effects for players to exploit till the get 'good effect'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-15-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:46:56-07:00","id":1129401,"title":"","content":"Man, you are stellar at pessimism.<br /> <br /> The effects of a palimpsest are unpredictable to the -character- and maybe the player. You should know as the ST exactly what you're doing with them and how to incorporate them into your game in a fun way.<br /> <br /> You're once again mischaracterising the Guardians, obviously. Guardians aren't against random things, and it's not immoral for things to be random or to experiment with those things that are. They would advocate caution, not wholesale shut down unless it turned out to be super bad. Heck, with their martyr complex they'd want to take most palimpsest for a test drive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-15-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:53:15-07:00","id":1129668,"title":"","content":"It's logical conclusion of the setting and game mechanics at play -<br /> IF:<br /> 1. Palimpsests effects are created randomly ( even if stable once determined for each item for each Palimpsests spell cast);<br /> 2. Players wants to cherry pick 'good effects' ( be honest here, most will want to );<br /> 3. Guardians will have some complaints if in one iteration effects are dangerous;<br /> 4. Creators Prime 3 characters are not bound for Mana limitation in longer time ( Channel Mana ) ...<br /> <br /> THEN:<br /> <b>All that depends on if item is 'bad' or 'good' for players is STs 'evilness'.</b> Typical discussion:<br /> - Player: 'Oh, I create Palimpsest for the next 3 days, casting it until I get things good for my character.'<br /> - ST ( having in mind good story plot ):'You spend three days, but on the last casting you only get Palimpsests that yes, it's Healing from your own Rote - but also subject is Turn into Stone.'<br /> - Player: 'What the hell, Mark?! Why can't we have our shinny things!?'<br /> <br /> And even if those discussion would be that at the table, and stranding players-STs relations, end result would be still:<br /> - Player: 'Whatever, I jus get extra Mana and cast Palimpsest spell to get nice item bonus this time'.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This mechanical solution with 'random effects' is:<br /> 1. Needlessly arbitrary on ST, leading to unneeded conflicts between players.<br /> AND/OR<br /> 2. Unneeded random for item creation, that ST need to prepare long list of 'special effects' that players will try on each spell iteration. 'Come, come, come dices - result 19 is the best!'<br /> AND TO ADD:<br /> 3. It's totally logical that 'spell echoes' most of the times carry over from previous version of Grimoire. If Supernal Magic is like science, previous impacts on the target ( Grimoire ) are staying on the target. If you are doing one chemical transformation of subject, results are staying with subject - If you put item in to Hydrochloric Acid - residues of acid stays on the item, don't they?<br /> <br /> <b>I can see, from time to time, truly 'random effects' of it ( mostly in story hooks department ) - but on day-to-day game running, going with 'spell echoes' variant is just more logical, stable, easier on ST-players tensions and quicker to do.</b> Also, if Palimpsests are semi-reliable ( 'About 90% just take over magic from previous book as spell echoes' ) Guardians would be totally for using them, only checking on those last dangerous possible dangerous elements - and if Guardians are happy, Mysterium can easily have full Athenea of Palimpsests, not everything locked in Censorium as they are unstable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Remember:</b> <i>To Orders, unstable means (possibly) dangerous - that's why they hate Abyss and Scelesti in the first place. Mages LOVES control ( that magic really is ) and random effects are opposition of control.<br /> <br /> Even Acanthus in 2E are more like strategists that 'wow, nice rainbow comes from my hands and fishes are flying!'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2017, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T23:11:44-07:00","id":1129697,"title":"","content":"It seems like your problems could easily be solved by just thinking up less jerky effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T00:17:25-07:00","id":1129704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129697#post1129697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like your problems could easily be solved by just thinking up less jerky effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>So cherry picking for players, even if rules are for made obviously to make random on each creation... Nothing wrong can happen on items creation for them, as they will get only positive effects, just because they are PCs, not NPCs.<br /> <br /> BUT assume I will be more generous to players and not get truly dangerous effects - we <i>still</i> will have cherry picking by players. Typical situation:<br /> <br /> - Player: 'I make Palimpsets for my Healing Rotes'.<br /> - ST: 'Okay, you got... Matter effect. So spells from Palimpsest will turn items around subject to be bigger.'<br /> - Player: ' Cool... but not cool enough. Let's try again.'<br /> - ST: 'Okay, you got... Fate effect. Good luck is forming about subject. Small bless for next scene after casting the spell.'<br /> - Player: ' Cool... but not cool enough. Tell me when we hit something truly outstanding. Or killing my enemies.'<br /> - ST: 'Ehhh...'<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T00:27:12-07:00","id":1129705,"title":"","content":"Whereas on 'spell echoes' ideas for powers you know that if you take for Palimpsest Grimoire about Forces control of fire - spells will, more or less, have effects on controlling of fire. And if you make your own Grimoire, you get Free Reach effect, as you are using the same Grimoire to make the Palimpsest on the same idea. AND you still can have whole Mystery angle about understanding what 'spell echoes' where before. AND you can easily and more believably trick Awakened into making Palimpsests from Abyssal Grimoire, as they are assuming that previous ( Abyssal ) Grimoire ( they did not know is Abyssal ) is just sure old tome with good spells.<br /> <br /> On random effects from Palimpsests it's just... random. And frustrating to run for Storyteller. As once I say before - I'm not against randomness effects from time to time, more as story hooks - like 1 on 10 Palimpsests have really random effect. But on the day to day using logical, better, faster and less irritating in gameplay is just using 'spell echoes' of previous Grimoire as base for Palimpsest. It's balancing act, but for me as Storyteller, crucial in running good games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T00:29:28-07:00","id":1129706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129704#post1129704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So cherry picking for players, even if rules are for made obviously to make random on each creation...</div> </div> </div> </div>The word &quot;random&quot; does not appear anywhere in the text and your characterizing this as &quot;cherry-picking&quot; does your understanding no favors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing wrong can happen on items creation for them, as they will get only positive effects, just because they are PCs, not NPCs. </div> </div> </div>They get positive effects because <i>that is what conjunctional Arcana do</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BUT assume I will be more generous to players and not get truly dangerous effects - we <i>still</i> will have cherry picking by players. Typical situation:<br /> <br /> - Player: 'I make Palimpsets for my Healing Rotes'.<br /> - ST: 'Okay, you got... Matter effect. So spells from Palimpsest will turn items around subject to be bigger.'<br /> - Player: ' Cool... but not cool enough. Let's try again.'<br /> - ST: 'Okay, you got... Fate effect. Good luck is forming about subject. Small bless for next scene after casting the spell.'<br /> - Player: ' Cool... but not cool enough. Tell me when we hit something truly outstanding. Or killing my enemies.'<br /> - ST: 'Ehhh...'<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>The solution to this is to not play with jackasses, whether you accomplish that through communication or choice of group composition.<br /> <br /> You might consider actually collaborating with your players to devise the additional effects and calibrate their expectations if you're so concerned about wasting your time on this kind of fruitless effort. This is an interpersonal system for a storytelling game, not an obligatory exchange that requires you to guess what obviously unreasonable standard your player has for adding peripheral effects to a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-16-2017, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T00:58:19-07:00","id":1129710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129706#post1129706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word &quot;random&quot; does not appear anywhere in the text and your characterizing this as &quot;cherry-picking&quot; does your understanding no favors.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Previewed spells write-up</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever a character later casts the rote from the completed Grimoire, it acts as though it incorporated dots of the chosen Arcanum equal to this spell's Potency, <b>creating unpredictable<br /> blended effects.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Unpredictable</b>, at least to my knowledge of English, is synonym word to random.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129706#post1129706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get positive effects because <i>that is what conjunctional Arcana do</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe truly I missed it - <b>Could you point me to official source that conjuntional Arcana always means benefit to the spell</b>? Last time I checked, most were transformations effects putted on the same item to change into other thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129706#post1129706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution to this is to not play with jackasses, whether you accomplish that through communication or choice of group composition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run this game 12 years, by 4 different groups as it is now - and in all <b>Mage </b>players sooner or later act as 'jackasses'. Part of the thing is that is ENCOURAGED by the setting, as Awakened are to become hubristic monsters in the end. But good mechanics against bad is there to not need to put those social stress on ST when it's really not needed and mechanics solve conflict issues. In this examples, 'unpredictable' Palimpsests are not really needed, generating players-ST conflicts where it's not working for story. Semi-relibale Palimpsests can also be source of Mysteries - as I pointed in my post above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129706#post1129706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might consider actually collaborating with your players to devise the additional effects and calibrate their expectations if you're so concerned about wasting your time on this kind of fruitless effort. This is an interpersonal system for a storytelling game, not an obligatory exchange that requires you to guess what obviously unreasonable standard your player has for adding peripheral effects to a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So cherry-pick for players just because they are PCs. Not too mention how many times should I let them - after 1, 2, 3... 10? How many NPCs are doing this kind of things till get the same effects like players? If players are cherry-picking, why not NPCs could not? Answer like 'it's you to decide as ST' is not really answer as we try to run consistent setting with both PCs and NPCs.<br /> <br /> I start to think most people talking in this discussion are not really STs that will run it on sessions-to-session basis - only players that play <b>Mage</b> games, and they always will be biased to get new shiny toys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2017, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T01:07:12-07:00","id":1129711,"title":"","content":"Healing spell which gets messed up by symbols of stone aren't limited to &quot;screw you, you're turned to stone&quot;. Like, the first thing i thought of was that it entombs the injured person in stone coffin and then slowly heals their wounds while they are safe in the coffin. It's a healing spell, but it's also a stone spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T01:20:19-07:00","id":1129714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129710#post1129710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unpredictable</b>, at least to my knowledge of English, is synonym word to random.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really, really isn't in any more than the most superficial sense \u2014 people can act &quot;unpredictably&quot; without acting randomly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe truly I missed it - Could you point me to official source that conjuntional Arcana always means benefit to the spell? Last time I checked, most were transformations effects putted on the same item to change into other thing. </div> </div> </div>Look at &quot;Add [Arcanum rating]&quot; sections in published spells instead of the most basic application of cross-Arcanum Patterning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I run this game now 12 years, by 4 different groups as it is now - and in all Mage players sooner or later act as 'jackasses'. </div> </div> </div>If your approach is not to stop them them when their direct response to not getting exactly what they wanted in a systems element representing a weird side-effect is overtly dismissive, ask them what kind of effects they'd want to see from such a system and take that under advisement, or do anything at all to steer their expectations to things you'd consider reasonable, then yes, the outcome will generally be indistinguishable from your players being utterly insufferable in that circumstance. This is generally considered to be a failure of execution on the part of the end-user.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So cherry-pick for players just because they are PCs. </div> </div> </div>Again, not doing yourself any favors by framing the issue like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many NPCs are doing this kind of things till get the same effects like players? </div> </div> </div>How many NPCs are fabricating grimoires, defacing them, re-enchanting them, and repeating the process ad infinitum is entirely down to how you have constructed your setting, but the world assumed by the books seems to function on the implication that the vast majority of mages have more interesting things to with their time than personally run a write-erase loop in the name of fishing for the equivalent of &quot;your Pocket Dimension has Twilight for spirits&quot; as an inbuilt function of a rote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If players are cherry-picking, why not NPCs could not? Answer like 'it's you to decide as ST' is not really answer as we try to run consistent setting. </div> </div> </div>If you-the-plural-entity-that-is-your-gaming-group try to run a &quot;consistent&quot; setting, you should have no trouble conferring with each other about whether a decision like what kind of weird effect your player's sideways rote gets serves the story you all are trying to tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I start to think most people talking in this discussion are not really STs that will run it on sessions-to-session basis - only players that play <b>Mage</b> games, and they always will be biased to get new shiny toys. </div> </div> </div>I've run more than twice as many games as I've been a player in, wyrd. Spare me this No True Scotsman tomfoolery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-16-2017, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:15:38-07:00","id":1129718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129710#post1129710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run this game 12 years, by 4 different groups as it is now - and in all <b>Mage </b>players sooner or later act as 'jackasses'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it happen only when you're running Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:24:09-07:00","id":1129720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129668#post1129668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Remember:</b>To Orders, unstable means (possibly) dangerous - that's why they hate Abyss and Scelesti in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is wrong on so many levels.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:37:47-07:00","id":1129731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129710#post1129710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unpredictable</b>, at least to my knowledge of English, is synonym word to random.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the issue, then, because the words are not even slightly synonyms. The concepts are only barely connected at all, in that something that is random is necessarily unpredictable, however there are an infinite number of ways something can be unpredictable without being random.<br /> <br /> If your issue is that 'No one would use these because the effects would be random and potentially harmful' when the text <b>doesn't actually say that</b>, only that they would be unpredictable...you're trying to solve a problem that exists only in your mind.<br /> <br /> The text establishes that they are unpredictable, and it establishes the implication that people want to use them. It follows that the effects are <b>not</b> random, nor potentially harmful, if that would cause mages in your setting to not want to use them. They are merely unpredictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:50:41-07:00","id":1129732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129711#post1129711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healing spell which gets messed up by symbols of stone aren't limited to &quot;screw you, you're turned to stone&quot;. Like, the first thing i thought of was that it entombs the injured person in stone coffin and then slowly heals their wounds while they are safe in the coffin. It's a healing spell, but it's also a stone spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's clearly interesting idea that I would go with as player - but it also the one half of players will not like on the 'oh, you are limiting us to be entombed in healing'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:16:55-07:00","id":1129740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129732#post1129732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's clearly interesting idea that I would go with as player - but it also the one half of players will not like on the 'oh, you are limiting us to be entombed in healing'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you talk about what would be cool with your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:36:50-07:00","id":1129743,"title":"","content":"I will try to concentrate on one thing I missed in running those rules - Add Arcanum Rating - than dwell by you all how bad ST I am simply by not liking mechanics that goes to me on ST-players conflict in gameplay that will go into needless loop of arguments or bad emotions at the game table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129714#post1129714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at &quot;Add [Arcanum rating]&quot; sections in published spells instead of the most basic application of cross-Arcanum Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Opening 2E corebook spells section&gt; Let's see... I compiled everything up to Space Arcanum spells effects.<br /> <br /> Add Death, Mind or Spirit - Spell is affecting ghosts, goetia or spirits or shitifn to particular Twilight frequancy, respectively.<br /> Add Time - Target to fast to gain Defense or change targets physical age.<br /> Add Matter \u2013 Gear changes with subject<br /> Add Mind 5 \u2013 Target gets true mind on it\u2019s own.<br /> Add Fate \u2013 Subject seems more important to those around.<br /> Add Time \u2013 Can detect <i>previous</i> parts of looked subject.<br /> Add Space \u2013 Gains awareness where subjects precisely are now.<br /> Add Forces - The subject is protected from extreme temperatures caused by the substance\u2019s state.<br /> Add Life \u2013 Spell is affecting living things or transform into living things. <br /> Add Forces \u2013 Spell transforms matter into plasm<br /> Add Life \u2013 Machines properties can be granted to living things<br /> Add Death or Spirit \u2013 Target get\u2019s Materialized Condition for the duration of spell<br /> Add Fate \u2013 Spell may affect target selectively<br /> Add Forces \u2013 Subject is not obviously magical<br /> Add Any Arcanum \u2013 Grants Mage Sight of the Arcanum<br /> <br /> If list of those Palimpsests effect would limited to those, they are non dangerous, I must admit. All are positive in some way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:39:09-07:00","id":1129744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129732#post1129732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's clearly interesting idea that I would go with as player - but it also the one half of players will not like on the 'oh, you are limiting us to be entombed in healing'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> Storytellers should know their group. It shouldn't be too hard to come up with a rote idea which would be interesting for your group. Maybe it's interesting because it's powerful, maybe it's interesting because of the unexpected features that you don't normally think up for spells, maybe it's a horrible spell butyour players want to find a use for it because of their respect for magic, maybe it's just weird and quirky, maybe it's a spell which conflicts with itself and the players want to study self-contradicting magic that doesn't invoke paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:40:46-07:00","id":1129745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1128791-signs-of-sorcery-open-dev-grimoires-why-use-palimpsests?p=1129718#post1129718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it happen only when you're running Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Only in Mage - in other games players are not spending 1/4 of game session to create superduper powerful magical solution to their problems, just using their few supernatural powers from their sheet - that in Obrimos players is most likely some come to creating some magical item they want to be 'perfect' and other end arguing on details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:45:08-07:00","id":1129842,"title":"","content":"But are they having fun? If they're willing to devote so much time to the magic system, perhaps they get something out of it. Or are you saying that they argue with you and put the session at a standstill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:09:27-07:00","id":1129919,"title":"","content":"Palimpsest creation sounds like a very mana and willpower intensive activity. First, you gotta spend the mana to create a grimoire, then you spend more mana to palimpsest them, and you gotta spend even more mana to make them both Lasting, or the rotes will evaporate when you release the spell or you have to release them with actual Willpower dots. You might even want to buy a rote or praxis for the spell, which costs Experiences, 'cause the Withstand on the most desirable and powerful rotes is not inconsiderable.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you don't quite know what the new effect is, you should probably scrutinize them thoroughly unless you are willing to cast the blindly (which is sometimes the case: Mages, hubris, shocked at gambling in this establishment), so that means more mana spent peeling back the opacity and willpower used to reveal.<br /> <br /> Palimpsest creation is not just any hobby, and demands considerable investment in time and resources. I wouldn't give anyone an unlimited amount of either in a Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:40:15-07:00","id":1129929,"title":"","content":"Mana intensive yes, WP intensive no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:21:20-07:00","id":1129950,"title":"","content":"&quot;Palimpsests farming&quot; is something I can totally see a character I want to run doing in her off screen time, but I also want to make her a Grimoire specialist who &quot;deals&quot; in copying grimoires and selling them to other people, so she will probably sell &quot;bad&quot; Palimpsests to mages interested in them. Like, I totally can see a Free Councilor spending 2 days of the week turning herself into grimoire copying machine, then palimpsetsting some of that, and then putting up some of them as &quot;mystery prizes&quot; in some sort of Free Council auctions.<br /> All while Guardians and Mysterium are shaking their fists from the outside next to the window, because the bouncer bounced them off :P. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:29:58-07:00","id":1129980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>A place for complicated spells.</b> The corebook (like the 1e core) doesn\u2019t have any spells that use more than one Arcanum in it, and although we tried our best, some spells didn\u2019t fit into its wordcount. Mages use their magic to investigate Mysteries, and those in this book are not exception. \u201cForge Thaumium\u201d and \u201cScribe Daimonomikon\u201d are both in here, as are means of affecting Yantras and specialized crafting magic.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I suspect this chapter of Signs will make &quot;coming up&quot; with Palimpsests much easier than it is with just core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}